llama.rs — Native Rust reimplementation of the llama.cpp inference engine.

This project is a from-scratch reimplementation, in pure Rust with no C/C++
code linked at runtime, of algorithms and behaviors of:

  llama.cpp — Copyright (c) 2026 ggml-org / Georgi Gerganov and contributors
  https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp — MIT License

Algorithm-level attribution to exact upstream source locations
(file:line of tag b12502, commit 398f00d65) is documented in
LLAMA_RS_ARCHITECTURE.md, section 2.

The files tests/parity/ref_q5.c and tests/parity/ref_q6.c are small
ground-truth harnesses transcribed from ggml/src/ggml-quants.c (MIT,
llama.cpp) and are used only as golden references in parity tests.

The parity test harness (tests/parity/run_parity.sh) compares llama.rs
outputs against upstream llama.cpp binaries as the golden reference.
